-- title:
--   Original stopped HJB expected dividend budget needs only nonpositive expected joint drift, rather than pathwise drift sign
-- statement:
--   On the genuine original Lévy X, admissible dividend D and ruin-stopped right-continuous bounded τ, with correct zero-clock piecewise terminal, exact complete inclusive Stieltjes cash, original q>0 and BV C1/UBV C2 HJB assumptions, a same-source one-sided stopped Ito estimate and integrable centred martingale imply both real and ENNReal expected discounted dividend bounds whenever the combined generator-plus-Stieltjes finite-variation drift is nonpositive *in expectation*. This weakens the previously Proved pointwise a.s. G+H≤0 hypothesis to E[G+H]≤0, matching the form of a source HJB drift integration. The one-sided Ito inequality itself remains explicit; no stochastic identity is smuggled.
-- source:
--   Avram Proposition 4(i), Eqs. (5.11)-(5.13); stronger probabilistic integration under only mean drift sign.

